pounded -23.1% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 4%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.1x, 6.4% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 4, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.4%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (14 sales, net $11.0M sold).","It returns 8.5% a year to shareholders (8.5% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 6.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 18.5% of the float, 7.0 days to cover."],"people":["With about 13,651 employees, each generates about $162K of revenue, 0.4x the Industrials median.","That works out to $4K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.8M (11x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":48,"head":"Watch: ROIC 5.0% vs WACC 7.5%.","pros":["Piotroski F-score 7/9","P/E 2.1x vs sector 24.1x","EV/EBITDA 7.1x vs sector 13.4x","5 analysts' mean target $42.20 (+35%)","12-1 month momentum +103%"],"cons":["ROIC 5.0% vs WACC 7.5%","Net debt/EBITDA 3.2x","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/FCF 51.2x vs sector 22.9x"],"flags":[],"need":["its composite (34) is below 39","only 2% below fair value","the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","it earns less than its cost of capital","too few checks pass (conviction 48)"],"buy_below":27.24,"vc":{"base":32.04,"base_src":"dcf","bear":17.31,"bull":55.22,"alt_median":20.59,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.5565,"dispersion":0.298,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","DCF is 56% above the other models' median ($20.59)","bull case is 3.2x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":24.0501,"ev_ebitda":13.39,"pfcf":22.9066,"pb":2.9489,"roic":0.0996,"gross